Consider the following $C$ function.
 For large values of $y$, the return value of the function $f$ best approximates
float f,(float x, int y) {
 float p, s; int i;
 for (s=1,p=1,i=1; i<y; i++) {
 p *= x/i;
 s += p;
 }
 return s;
}

